menu "SKAFTSARV Light"

    menu "LED strip"

        config SKAFT_LED_GPIO
            int "WS281x data GPIO"
            range 0 30
            default 2
            help
                GPIO driving the strip's data line (the brown wire in a stock
                SKAFTSARV). 2 is pad D2 on the XIAO ESP32-C6.

                GPIO3 and GPIO14 are wired to the board's FM8625H RF switch and
                must never be used for anything else.

        config SKAFT_LED_COUNT
            int "Number of LEDs on the strip"
            range 1 300
            default 30
            help
                A stock IKEA SKAFTSARV has 30.

        config SKAFT_LED_RMT_CHANNEL
            int "RMT TX channel"
            range 0 1
            default 0
            help
                The ESP32-C6 has two RMT channels capable of transmit. Nothing
                else in this firmware uses RMT.

        config SKAFT_LED_MEM_BLOCKS
            int "RMT memory blocks for the strip channel"
            range 1 2
            default 2
            help
                Each C6 RMT channel owns 48 symbol words; one WS281x bit costs one
                symbol. The legacy RMT driver refills the block from an ISR that
                competes with the 802.15.4 radio, and a missed refill latches the
                strip mid-frame (a visible flicker). Claiming both TX blocks gives
                96 symbols, about 120 us of buffer instead of 60 us.

                Set to 1 only if you need the second RMT TX channel for something else.

    endmenu

    menu "Rendering"

        config SKAFT_RENDER_FPS
            int "Effect frame rate (frames per second)"
            range 10 100
            default 50
            help
                Only animated effects redraw at this rate; a solid colour is sent
                once and then the strip is left alone.

        config SKAFT_GAMMA_X10
            int "Dimming gamma, times 10"
            range 10 30
            default 22
            help
                Gamma applied to the brightness level before it scales the colour,
                as a fixed-point value: 22 means gamma 2.2. Linear 8-bit dimming on
                a WS281x collapses the bottom of the range into a handful of visible
                steps. Set to 10 for no correction.

    endmenu

    menu "Colour temperature"

        config SKAFT_CT_MIN_KELVIN
            int "Warmest colour temperature (K)"
            range 1000 6500
            default 2000
            help
                Reported to Matter as ColorTempPhysicalMaxMireds. The strip has no
                white LEDs, so colour temperature is approximated as tinted white.

        config SKAFT_CT_MAX_KELVIN
            int "Coolest colour temperature (K)"
            range 2000 10000
            default 6500
            help
                Reported to Matter as ColorTempPhysicalMinMireds.

    endmenu

    config SKAFT_ENABLE_CONSOLE
        bool "Enable the USB-serial debug console"
        default y
        help
            A small esp_console REPL on the USB-Serial-JTAG port for bench-testing
            the strip and forcing a factory reset. See main/app_console.c.

    config SKAFT_USE_EXTERNAL_ANTENNA
        bool "Use the external U.FL antenna"
        default n
        help
            The XIAO ESP32-C6 routes its radio through an FM8625H RF switch: GPIO3
            enables the switch, GPIO14 picks the antenna. Enable this only if a U.FL
            antenna is physically fitted. A board inside a plastic lamp body is
            normally fine on the onboard ceramic antenna, which is the default.

    config ENABLE_MEMORY_PROFILING
        bool "Enable Memory Profiling"
        default n
        help
            Enable this option to include memory profiling features in the example.
            This will allow you to monitor memory usage during runtime.

endmenu
